 to  upset her maybe just maybe  doesn't have any parents at all because  she's one of a whole bunch of clones  made for the purpose of fighting in the  Galactic war perhaps her sisters are all  evil while raised the sole clone who  malfunctioned and joined the light side  or maybe she's not a clone maybe she had  a twin with race parents having sold her  sister immediately after their births  the abandoned twin might have grown  vengeful and turned to the dark side and  the evil ray we see could be that  scorned sister another theory is that  dark ray isn't real in the slightest and  that what we're seeing in the rise of  skywalker clip is part of a sort of  dream sequence just as luke skywalker  saw himself as his father Darth Vader  while inside the Dagobah cave and the  Empire Strikes Back  Rey could have a similar vision in the  rise of Skywalker facing her biggest  fear in watching herself turned to the  dark side this could give her the push  she needs to continue fighting against  the first order when the temptation to  turn dark grows too strong there are  about a billion possible explanations  for what's going on here and the same  can be said for what looks like an evil  version of c-3po in the newly released  rise of Skywalker footage the protocol  droid known for his etiquette and  intelligence is seen here with glowing  red eyes that's the only physical  attribute of his to suggest that the  upcoming film features a dark c-3po and  while we hate to make sweeping  generalizations and saying that every  character with red eyes is evil there's  evidence to suggest that this could be  the case here things like that in  February 2015 Marvel Comics rolled out a  new Darth Vader series which revealed an  issue number 3 that the heavy breathing  dark Sider had in his entourage droids  that have the same design as c-3po and  r2d2 there's triple zero essentially an  evil version of c-3po from a design  perspective and bt1 and assassin droids  that recalls the design of r2d2 these  robots are battle droids designed to  kill which is a far cry from how helpful  Threepio and r2 generally are  speculation has it that the red eyed  c-3po shown in the rise of skywalker  footage could actually be triple 0 and  that the skywalker who rises in the new  movie  is anakin who may return as a force  ghost with his literal killing machines  in tow  since additional footage from the rise  of skywalker shown at a disney  shareholders meeting in March 2019  reportedly featured kylo Ren opening a  container that holds Darth Vader's  helmet it's not completely out of the  realm of possibility that the villain  formerly known as Anakin Skywalker could  play a part in the upcoming film on the  other hand maybe the explanation for the  evil c-3po is simple perhaps the reason  why the Droid has red eyes during that  scene is because he has had his  personality inadvertently augmented to  be extra aggressive for the sake of  comedy sort of like what happens to  data's emotion chip and Star Trek yes I  hate this all this is to say that many  mysteries still surround the rise of  Skywalker and hardly any concrete  answers are on hand right now writer and  director JJ Abrams could have taken the  film in any number of different  directions making it all the more  difficult to pin down which theories  could be true and which are total BS the  rise of Skywalker will surely answer the  big questions about dark gray in the  potentially dark c-3po but fans will  have to be content with waiting until  the film's release on December 20th to  learn the truth check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite films  are coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

